Bugs:
On the subject of bugs - if you overeat a corpse and get confused while
eating it , you die instead of getting the "Stop Eating? " message. 
Fair enough, but I had an amulet of life saving on at the time. Upon 
resurrection , however, the character was still confused, and still
continued eating the corpse, and so immediately croaked once more.

.... Seemed a bit unfair at the time 

Suggestions for further releases:
1) They say some of the levels of hell are icy cold.

2) Intoduce more terrain features eg. Underwater levels, Cloud Islands,
   Above Ground Areas.

3) Expand on monster abilities/immunities:  Eg: Sightless monsters should
   not be affected by your being invisible.  Golems should be immune to
   (most) magic attacks - eg conflict, damage from spells/wands. 
   Magically resistant creatures (liches etc) should also have a chance
   of being immune to conflict.  It seems to me hack is too easy once
   you've got a ring of conflict.

4) Allow healing spells/devices to be applied to pets (Eg Allow zapping
   a healing spell in a chosen direction).

5) More special levels such as the castle please (that was fun the first
   few times). Vlad's Castle was too small to be a challenge, although
   the idea was good. (Eg Multi-level underwater shipwreck)

6) How about an SF version of Hack?

